    {
      "filename": "Saturn V Dynamic Test Configurations.png",
      "title": "File:Saturn V Dynamic Test Configurations.png",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/Saturn_V_Dynamic_Test_Configurations.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_V_Dynamic_Test_Configurations.png",
      "width": 601,
      "height": 768,
      "mime": "image/png",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "NASA",
      "description": "Saturn V dynamic testing was conducted in three configurations:\nConfiguration I simulates the flight vehicle configuration during the first phase of flight, when the first stage, S-IC provides thrust, and is made up of the S-IC-D, the S-II-S/D, the S-IVB-D stages, the S-IU-200D/500D instrument unit and the BP-027 spacecraft.\nConfiguration II simulates the flight vehicle configuration during the second phase of flight, when the second stage, S-II  provides thrust, and is made up of the S-II-S/D, S-IVB-D, the S-IU-200D/500D and the BP-27.\n\nConfiguration III simulates the flight vehicle configuration during the third phase of flight, when the third stage, S-IVB  provides thrust, and is made up of S-IVB-D, the S-IU-200D/500D and the BP-27.",
      "dateCreated": "1965-04-16",
